# One skill of the interaction intelligence, asked by a Behavior Tree: a question to the LLM
# (understand an utterance, phrase a reply) or an operation on the data of the dialogue.
# The intelligence keeps no state: the state of the dialogue (JSON) comes in and goes out.
string dialogue_id
string skill
string state
string user_text
# Skill-specific inputs: a word (e.g. who ended a roleplay), a number (e.g. the attempts so
# far) and a JSON object (the request, for "begin")
string option
int32 number
string args
# The time the skill may still spend waiting for the model (s): what is left of the time budget
# of the reply being prepared (reply_budget after a user turn, opening_budget for the opening).
# Once it is spent, the skill's remaining questions to the model fail at once and the skill
# answers with its fallbacks. 0 = no budget: each call to the model waits at most llm_timeout
float64 budget_s
---
bool success
# Why the skill failed
string message
string state
# What the robot must say, if anything
string reply
# What the skill found, for the tree to decide (e.g. "complete", "confirms", "unclear")
string label
# The phase of the dialogue and its data (the result so far), as JSON
string phase
string data
